L({ key: 'agent-pull-loop-inbox-checkout', domains: ['agent-bridge', 'handoff'], layer: 'content',
  what: 'The agent skill defines the work loop: GET /agents/me → GET /agents/me/inbox-lite → pick by status priority → checkout → GET /issues/:id/heartbeat-context (compact state, ancestors, comment cursor) → work → PATCH status with a comment → release. SPEC: "The heartbeat is a protocol, not a runtime."',
  notable: 'If the agent pulls its own work, the server can be a stateless API: the agent's own scheduler (OpenClaw heartbeat or cron) runs the loop, so nothing on Cloudflare has to hold connections or timers, and the bridge becomes optional (only for instant wake). The compact inbox-lite and heartbeat-context views are hand-made for agents to save tokens; a generated CRUD API needs these few agent views next to it.',
