  what: 'Paperclip calls itself "the control plane, not the execution plane", but now ships its own runtime: a native Rust Runner that supervises agent CLIs on the host (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini, Kimi, Pi, Cursor) plus built-in agents. External gateway agents such as OpenClaw are second class: hidden from the agent picker (hideFromVisualSelection, "Invite external agents"), with every UI capability off (no instructions bundle, no skills sync, no model choice).',
  notable: 'Using Paperclip with AICoworker means running two runtimes, and the one fgOPC actually uses (OpenClaw) gets the weakest integration and breaks on protocol bumps. Either let Paperclip be the runtime and drop AICoworker for these agents, or keep AICoworker as the only runtime and use a thin control plane in which OpenClaw is first class — the original schema-first Cloudflare plan.',
