add('agent-bridge.yaml', { key: 'daemon-ws-wake-plus-poll', domains: ['agent-bridge', 'storage-sync'], layer: 'content',
  what: 'A Multica daemon runs on the user machine next to the agent CLIs and dials an outbound WebSocket to the server. The server pushes a wake hint when work is waiting, the daemon claims tasks for all its runtimes in one batch, a 30-second poll is the catch-up path, and heartbeats go every 15 seconds. RPC over the WebSocket falls back to HTTP only when the frame was not sent; if it was sent but the outcome is unknown it must not retry on another transport, to avoid a double claim.',
  notable: 'This is the fgOPC bridge design, proven in production: outbound only (no open ports, works behind NAT), push for speed, poll so a missed push never loses work, and an explicit rule against double claims. On Cloudflare the server side is a Durable Object holding the daemon sockets; the daemon is the small non-LLM waker on the AICoworker host.',
